{"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"PropertyGraph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PropertyGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08PropertyA0P","roleHeading":"Protocol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PropertyGraph"}]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/propertygraph"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph"},"abstract":[{"text":"A graph that keeps maps from its vertices and edges to values.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/EdgePosition","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/Vertex"],"title":"Associated Types","anchor":"Associated-Types"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/addEdgeMap(default:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/addEdgeMap(of:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/addVertexMap(default:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/addVertexMap(of:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/removeEdgeMap(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/removeVertexMap(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/values(of:)-2ufmp","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/values(of:)-89n40"],"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/subscript(_:checked:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/subscript(_:checkedEdgeAt:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/subscript(_:checkedVertexAt:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/subscript(_:of:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/subscript(_:ofEdgeAt:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/subscript(_:ofVertexAt:)"],"title":"Subscripts","anchor":"Subscripts"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PropertyGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08PropertyA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The graph owns the values and keeps every attached map in step with its mutations. The caller","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"holds a small handle, ","type":"text"},{"code":"VertexMap<Value>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"EdgeMap<Value>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each map has a default value, which every element has until it is given another, so a new"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element needs no write. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"addEdgeMap(default: 1.0)"},{"type":"text","text":" is a map of weights that are all 1."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"addEdgeMap(of: T.self)"},{"type":"text","text":" is a map of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T?"},{"type":"text","text":" whose default is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every mutation updates every attached map in the same call. A removed element’s value goes with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, and a representation that moves another element into the hole (a swap-remove) moves that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element’s values too. Removing a vertex removes its edges’ values. Reading or writing the value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of a removed element traps. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checked"},{"type":"text","text":" subscripts throw "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"VertexNotFound"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EdgeNotFound"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeAll"},{"type":"text","text":" empties every map and keeps it attached, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeAllEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" empties the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge maps."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A handle is valid on the graph that attached it and on every copy, until ","type":"text"},{"code":"removeVertexMap(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or ","type":"text"},{"code":"removeEdgeMap(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Using it on any other graph traps. It also works through a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"GraphAdaptor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of that graph, which reads the base’s values, and through a ","type":"text"},{"code":"GraphDelegator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which reads and writes them. Writing a map value is not a structural mutation and does not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"advance ","type":"text"},{"code":"generation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A copy of the graph shares every map. The first write to a map, or structural mutation, of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copy copies the map’s storage: a dense map all at once, like an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a paged map a page","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at a time.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Equality, hashing, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" and descriptions ignore maps. Equal graphs may carry different"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"maps, a decoded graph has none, and a conversion to another representation carries none."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns a snapshot of a map that reads as fast as an array. Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{ w[$0] }"},{"type":"text","text":" where"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an algorithm asks for a weight closure:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let weights = graph.addEdgeMap(default: 1.0)","\/\/ … set some weights …","let w = graph.values(of: weights)","let distances = graph.dijkstraShortestPaths(from: start, weight: { w[$0] })"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The snapshot does not check liveness. At a removed position it reads an unspecified value,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"either the default or the value the element had. Algorithms read only the values of live","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements, so each read stays one load.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/PropertyGraph/Vertex":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/propertygrap